hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"151","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his head after the second bowing (ruku‘), he supplicated: “O Allah! Rescue Walid bin Walid (the brother of Khalid bin Walid, may Allah be pleased with him), Salamah bin Hisham, ‘Ayyash bin Abi Rabi‘ah, and the weak Muslims from the captivity of the disbelievers of Makkah. O Allah! Crush the disbelievers of the tribe of Mudar with severity, and inflict upon them a famine like the famine during the time of Yusuf (peace be upon him).”"
"152","Muhammad bin Sirin (may Allah have mercy on him) says: I asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) about Qunoot. He replied that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Qunoot after bowing (ruku‘)."
"153","‘Ubad bin Tamim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his uncle that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he feels doubt in prayer that wind has passed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not leave the prayer unless you hear a sound or perceive a smell.”"
